      "id": "qa_1750727986766_svpns052",
      "question": "Mbbs",
      "answer": "For MBBS admissions at KGMU, the process typically involves:\n\n1.  **Eligibility:** You must have passed the 10+2 examination with Physics, Chemistry, Biology, and English. You also need to qualify for the NEET-UG exam.\n2.  **NEET-UG:** You must appear for and qualify for the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET-UG).\n3.  **Counseling:** Based on your NEET-UG score, you'll be eligible for counseling conducted by the relevant authorities.\n4.  **Registration and Choice Filling:** You'll need to register for the counseling process and fill in your choices of colleges, including KGMU.\n5.  **Seat Allotment:** Seats are allotted based on your NEET-UG rank, choices filled, and availability of seats.\n6.  **Admission:** If you are allotted a seat at KGMU, you must complete the admission process, which involves document verification and fee payment.\n\nFor more detailed and up-to-date information, it's best to check the following resources:\n\n*   **KGMU Official Website:** [www.kgmu.org](http://www.kgmu.org) (Look for the \"Courses/Admission\" section.)\n*   **NEET-UG Official Website:** (Search for the official NEET-UG website for the latest updates on the exam, counseling, and admission process.)\n*   **Medical Counselling Committee (MCC) Website:** (For information on the counseling process.)\n\nPlease note that the admission process and criteria are subject to change, so it's essential to refer to the official sources for the most accurate and current information.\n",
