      "question": "Kitne number pe Mil jayega",
      "answer": "The number of marks needed to get admission to MBBS at KGMU depends on several factors, including:\n\n*   **The year of admission:** The cut-off marks change every year based on the difficulty of the NEET-UG exam and the number of applicants.\n*   **Category:** The cut-off marks vary for different categories like General, OBC, SC, ST, and EWS.\n*   **Number of seats available:** The total number of MBBS seats at KGMU also influences the cut-off.\n*   **Competition:** The overall performance of the candidates in the NEET-UG exam affects the cut-off scores.\n\nI cannot provide a specific number as the cut-off marks change annually. However, you can get an idea by looking at the previous years' cut-off marks. You can find this information on the official KGMU website, the NEET-UG official website, or through counseling websites.\n",
