      "answer": "As I mentioned before, I cannot predict the exact cut-off marks for the General category for the 2025 admissions. However, to get an idea, you should:\n\n1.  **Check Previous Years' Cut-offs:** Look at the cut-off marks for the General category for the past few years (2023, 2022, etc.) on the KGMU website, NEET-UG official website, or counseling websites. This will give you a general idea of the score range.\n2.  **Consider the Trend:** Analyze the trend in cut-off marks over the past few years. Has it been increasing, decreasing, or staying relatively stable?\n3.  **Estimate Based on Competition:** The difficulty level of the NEET-UG exam and the overall performance of the candidates in 2025 will impact the cut-off.\n4.  **Aim High:** It's always best to aim for a score higher than the previous year's cut-off to increase your chances of getting admission.\n\nKeep in mind that this is just an estimate, and the actual cut-off marks for 2025 may vary.\n",
